sessionalHymns.text:
When Thou didst appear in the flesh for baptism, O Invisible One,
Jordan ministered to Thee with its streams, and John stretched forth his corruptible hand;
yet the one turned back in fear, and the other straightway touched Thee the Incorruptible One, with trembling.
Truly Thou art the Lamb of God, the ever-living Fountain Who hath sanctified the springs, the sea and all mankind;
for the Trinity shone forth from on high://
the Father calleth Thee His Son, and the Holy Spirit descendeth.

ode4.irmos:
I hymn Thee, O Lord, for I have heard report of Thee, and I was afraid;
for Thou comest to me, seeking me who am lost.//
Wherefore, I glorify Thy great condescension towards me, O greatly Merciful One.

exapostilarion.text:
Thou didst wondrously prepare the ways of the Lord;
for thou wast the herald of His coming, the preacher most true and the greatest of the prophets, O blessed John.//
Thou didst behold the Light, fulfilling His ineffable dispensation.
